{"UserSerializer defines include_website_name without a trailing ? so serializer inclusion conventions won't treat it as a conditional include hook, causing website_name to be emitted regardless of website presence/restrictions": 0.5470799207687378, "UserSerializer serializes website_name for all viewers but it is not part of untrusted_attributes gating, exposing user's website host/path even when website itself is hidden under restrictions for TL0/anonymous users": 0.9385141134262085, "website_name compares Discourse.current_hostname directly to URI(...).host but current_hostname may include a :port suffix, causing same-domain/parent-domain detection to fail on installations running behind a non-default port": 0.30321556329727173, "On line 149, \".\" << website_host uses the << operator which mutates the string literal \".\" in place, which will raise a FrozenError if frozen_string_literal: true is ever added to this file": 0.25646156072616577, "website_name method fails to show full URL path when user's website is a subdomain of the Discourse instance's domain because the else branch only checks if Discourse host is a child of website host, never the reverse": 0.6833051443099976, "Domain matching logic incorrectly assumes all 3-part domains consist of a 1-part subdomain and 2-part root domain, breaking for 2-part TLDs like .co.uk, causing unrelated domains like example.co.uk and other.co.uk to be treated as the same domain": 0.8096392750740051, "website_name method parses website.to_s string into a URI object multiple times per execution instead of caching the parsed URI object once": 0.03223898634314537}